# Copy this file to config/pro.env and paste your Ubuntu Pro token.
# From the repo folder in a terminal, that's:
#   cp config/pro.env.example config/pro.env
# Then open config/pro.env in any text editor (e.g. "nano config/pro.env";
# in nano, save with Ctrl+O then Enter, and exit with Ctrl+X).
# Get the token at https://ubuntu.com/pro/dashboard (a free personal token works).
# Replace only the text between the quotes, and keep the quotes.
# config/pro.env is git-ignored, so your token never gets committed (uploaded).
#
# Every lab VM (the server and each client) is attached to Ubuntu Pro with this
# token, which Landscape needs for registration. The lab uses 4 machines; a
# free personal token allows 5. scripts/99-cleanup.sh detaches each VM before
# deleting it, so rebuilding the lab doesn't use up your token's machines.
UBUNTU_PRO_TOKEN="PASTE_YOUR_PRO_TOKEN_HERE"
